=\frac{\cos^{2}\theta-\sin^{2}\theta}{(\cos\theta+\sin\theta)^{2}}
=\frac{\cos\theta-\sin\theta}{\cos\theta+\sin\theta}
=\frac{-2\sin\theta-\sin\theta}{-2\sin\theta+\sin\theta}=3\]故选 A.

